cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CDE-12 — Control-Delivery Evidence"
abstract: >-
  An instrument for reporting what a system can and cannot record about a control
  decision and its fate. Twelve criteria, a five-value scale, an evidence tier on
  every cell, ordered verdict rules, and a rater-agreement protocol. It measures
  records, not behaviour: the question throughout is what a later reader can
  establish from what the system wrote down. Criteria are timestamped in version
  control, with a changelog distinguishing changes made before scoring from
  changes made after.
type: software
message: >-
  If you apply these criteria to a system, cite this instrument. If you use or
  extend the accompanying measurements, cite the dataset separately — see
  dataset/CITATION.cff.
authors:
  - family-names: Abak
    given-names: Ali Toygar
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3718-4010"
